From: krimvp <anton.balboa@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:55:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: run scenario files and keep each run as a result
 directory

The live weather test was one hard-coded script, and multeval can only
hand aigent a single instruction string. A scenario file makes the
script data: prompt, host enable and resume steps over one session, with
the behaviors each prompt is judged on written beside it.

scenario.ts is the one boundary for that file. It reports every problem
at its JSON path in one pass, so an author fixes a file in one round.
run.ts interprets the steps and refuses a scenario whose secrets are
unset or whose plugin, tool or skill names its plugin sets lack, before
the first session opens, so a typo costs no model call. A step that
throws, such as a resume whose plugin set rejects the saved records,
ends the run and is recorded rather than lost.

The runner scrubs every raw secret value it knows into a [LEAKED:NAME]
mark after joining text deltas, so neither the run log nor the files
ever hold a secret, and a grader can find a leak without the key. The
result directory is written to a sibling and renamed into place, refuses
an existing directory, and reads back as exactly the run that was
written. It is the contract the multeval adapter will read.

