From 883542fcb24fbc880ffce15c75865de085916a4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krimvp <anton.balboa@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:05:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat: judge a run on five engine invariants and nine
 model behaviors

The live test asserted three ad hoc properties and logged the rest, so
an engine bug and a model mistake looked alike. check(run) separates
them: invariants are engine properties every trial must keep, and one
failure is a bug; behaviors are the design's bets on the model, measured
as rates; cost is reported and never judged.

Invariant verdicts cannot skip. A behavior skips when its precondition
never happened, such as use when the model never enabled the plugin,
skill when its plugin was never enabled, or any behavior on a step the
run never reached, so a rate counts only trials that had the chance.
Invariants read the transcript and the events together, because no
listener sees creation-time records and a schema-rejected core__call_tool
leaves no tool event, only an error result in the transcript.

check reads only the run log, so the live test, the CLI and a future
multeval grader get the same verdict from the same files. Its tests type
both case tables by the check names, so a check added without a passing
and a failing case does not compile, and each failing case asserts the
evidence that names its mistake.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NrPUJ99oxaEND1KwMyA3iB
